@startuml fig12_package
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 12 — Package View: The Shared-Policy Invariant

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 60

package "configs" {
  [experiment YAML + seeds\none file per run] as C
}

package "harness" #FFFCF5 {
  [gen_trace.py  ·  replay.py\nmanifest.py  ·  logging_jsonl.py] as H
}

package "live" {
  [scheduler.py  ·  capability_view.py\nworker.py — one runtime, llama.cpp  ·  client.py] as L
}

package "sim" #FFFCF5 {
  [des.py  ·  sim_node.py\nservice_time.py] as S
}

package "policies" {
  [dispatch_policy.py — interface: choose(request, node_states, now, rng)\nround_robin  ·  jsq  ·  static_weighted  ·  wjsq  ·  threshold\ncost_model.py — lookup table / <= 6-parameter regression] as P
}

package "analysis" #FFFCF5 {
  [join.py  ·  metrics.py\nfigures.py  ·  validate.py] as A
}

C ..> H : parameterises
C ..> S : parameterises
H ..> L : drives, open loop
H ..> S : same trace (F-17)
L .[#B45309].> P : **imports**
S .[#B45309].> P : **imports**
L ..> A : per-process records
S ..> A : per-process records
H ..> A : run manifest

note right of P
  **The invariant of the study.** `live` and `sim` both depend on
  `policies`; `policies` depends on neither, and imports no clock,
  no socket and no global RNG. A policy is therefore never
  reimplemented for the simulator, and a simulated result travels
  the same code path as a hardware result (F-21).
end note

note bottom of A
  Consumes only the joined record set, so hardware runs and simulated
  runs are analysed by identical code and are directly comparable —
  the precondition for the validation criterion of F-23.
end note
@enduml
